<article class="env-lemma" id="02V8">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02V8">Lemma <span data-tag="02V8">39.3.2</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $U$ be a scheme over $S$. Let $j : R \to U \times _ S U$ be a pre-relation. Let $g : U' \to U$ be a morphism of schemes. Finally, set </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  R' = (U' \times _ S U')\times _{U \times _ S U} R \xrightarrow {j'} U' \times _ S U'  \]
</div>
  <p> Then $j'$ is a pre-relation on $U'$ over $S$. If $j$ is a relation, then $j'$ is a relation. If $j$ is a pre-equivalence relation, then $j'$ is a pre-equivalence relation. If $j$ is an equivalence relation, then $j'$ is an equivalence relation. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
